---
# Conservative default per docs/design/00-requirements.md §7.4: broad checks on,
# with a short, explicit suppression list for rules that fight hand-written
# low-level numerics code (bit manipulation in the RNG, fixed-size buffers in
# the streaming path generator). Two more suppressions added in Phase 2, based
# on an actual local clang-tidy run rather than guessing ahead of time:
# cppcoreguidelines-init-variables false-positives on every `const double x =
# expr;` (it's meant for genuinely uninitialized declarations); and
# bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters, which flags essentially every pricer
# signature in this codebase (S, K, r, q, sigma, T is the universal quant
# finance parameter order, not an accident risk worth a warning here).
Checks: >
  bugprone-*,
  cppcoreguidelines-*,
  modernize-*,
  performance-*,
  -modernize-use-trailing-return-type,
  -cppcoreguidelines-avoid-magic-numbers,
  -readability-magic-numbers,
  -cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-pointer-arithmetic,
  -cppcoreguidelines-avoid-non-const-global-variables,
  -cppcoreguidelines-init-variables,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters
WarningsAsErrors: ''
HeaderFilterRegex: '.*/include/mcd/.*'
FormatStyle: file
